Source: flickos-media
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-media
Architecture: all
# playerctl: the follower watches the players with one playerctl --follow and
# the buttons run it. cava: the spectrum's sound analysis (244 KB, with
# libiniparser4 and SDL2 about 2.4 MB in the image). python3-gi,
# gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1: the spectrum strip, only while it
# shows. python3-gi-cairo: its drawing, and clicks go through it.
# flickos-layouts (>= 1.66): the panel modules (custom/media-*), inserted
# while controls is on, their icons in base.css and the scrolling title's
# fixed width. pipewire-bin: pw-dump, whether a player that says it plays
# makes a sound (already in the image: flickos-screenshot's pw-play).
Depends: python3,
         playerctl,
         pipewire-bin,
         cava,
         python3-gi,
         python3-gi-cairo,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1,
         flickos-layouts (>= 1.66),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: media controls and a sound spectrum for the FlickOS panel
 Previous, play or pause, next and the title of what is playing, in the
 FlickOS panel while an app plays music or video. A spectrum that moves with
 the sound can be shown just above the panel, behind windows or over them;
 clicks go through it.
 .
 Off by default: turned on in Settings > Media Controls, and nothing of it
 runs while off.
